4. Constraints Silently Optimize Your Queries 
Foreign Keys are not just for data integrity. They act as hidden performance boosters. 

• If you join two massive tables together but your SELECT clause only pulls columns from the primary table, the query optimizer uses Join Elimination. 
• Because the foreign key guarantees a matching row exists, the database engine completely removes the JOIN from the actual execution plan, saving immense amounts of memory and I/O overhead.  

